<article dtd-version="1.3" article-type="meeting-abstract" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="hwp">ascomtg</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="pmc">ascomtg</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">ASCOMTG</journal-id><journal-title-group><journal-title>Journal of Clinical Oncology</journal-title><abbrev-journal-title>ASCO MEETING ABSTRACTS</abbrev-journal-title></journal-title-group><issn pub-type="ppub">0732-183X</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1527-7755</issn><publisher><publisher-name>American Society of Clinical Oncology</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="custom" custom-type="meeting-id">335</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="custom" custom-type="session-id">17304</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="custom" custom-type="session-participation-id">8020500</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="custom" custom-type="temporary-abstract-id">24701</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="custom" custom-type="abstract-id">rw24701</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3727/096504017X14982578608217</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Biochemistry</subject></subj-group><series-title>2026 ASCO Annual Meeting (May 29 - June 2, 2026)</series-title><series-text>Publication Only</series-text></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Dexmedetomidine Inhibits Osteosarcoma Cell Proliferation and Migration, and Promotes Apoptosis by Regulating miR-520a-3p</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib id="C8020500" contrib-type="presenter"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>Xiaoyan</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A8020500" /></contrib><contrib id="C8020501" contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>Yongguang</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A8020500" /></contrib><contrib id="C8020502" contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Xinlei</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A8020500" /></contrib><contrib id="C8020503" contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Xiao</surname><given-names>Jianmin</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A8020500" /></contrib><aff id="A8020500">Department of Anesthesiology, Shandong Provincial Hospital Affiliated With Shandong University, Jinan, Shandong, P.R. China; Department of Anesthesiology, Ningjin People’s Hospital, Ningjin, Shandong, P.R. China;</aff></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>2018</year></pub-date><fpage>rw24701</fpage><lpage>rw24701</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>ASCO-style conversion for internal testing; source rights remain with the original publisher.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2018</copyright-year></permissions><abstract><p><bold>rw24701</bold></p><p>This study aimed to investigate the effect of dexmedetomidine (DEX) on osteosarcoma (OS) cell line MG63 and to explore the possible relationship between DEX and miR-520-3p in OS. The results showed that DEX could upregulate miR-520-3p, which directly targeted AKT1 . Additionally, miR-520-3p also inhibited MG63 cell proliferation and migration, promoted apoptosis, and suppressed protein expressions of AKT, p-AKT, p-mTOR, and p-ERK1/2. DEX can inhibit OS cell proliferation and migration and promote apoptosis by upregulating the expression level of miR-520a-3p. DEX may serve as a potential therapeutic agent in OS treatment, and miR-520a-3p may be a potential target in the therapy of OS.</p></abstract><custom-meta-group><custom-meta><meta-name>source-row-number</meta-name><meta-value>205</meta-value></custom-meta><custom-meta><meta-name>source-record-id</meta-name><meta-value>24701.0</meta-value></custom-meta><custom-meta><meta-name>source-journal</meta-name><meta-value>Oncology Research Featuring Preclinical and Clinical Cancer Therapeutics</meta-value></custom-meta><custom-meta><meta-name>source-publisher</meta-name><meta-value>Cognizant Communication Corporation</meta-value></custom-meta><custom-meta><meta-name>source-country</meta-name><meta-value>China</meta-value></custom-meta><custom-meta><meta-name>source-article-type</meta-name><meta-value>Research Article;</meta-value></custom-meta><custom-meta><meta-name>manual-verdict</meta-name><meta-value>YES</meta-value></custom-meta><custom-meta><meta-name>source-reason</meta-name><meta-value>Investigation by Third Party;Notice - Limited or No Information;Paper Mill;Removed;</meta-value></custom-meta></custom-meta-group></article-meta></front></article>
